10 CLI Reference
****************

The ‘bin/hell’ CLI provides complete environment management:
‘sync’
     Download, build, and byte-compile all active packages and language
     servers.
‘upgrade’
     Pull latest Hell Emacs git commits/tags, update packages, and
     re-sync.
‘config’
     Inspect and add newly introduced default modules (‘config
     --add-defaults’).
‘doctor’
     Comprehensive health verification of Emacs, SDKs, JDKs, servers,
     and tools.
‘profile’
     List and sync multi-profile environments (‘profile list’, ‘profile
     sync --all’).
‘plugins’
     Manage community and third-party modules (‘plugins list’, ‘plugins
     enable’).
‘bundle’
     Create self-contained offline deployment packages.
‘doctor --network’
     Validate connectivity through configured proxies, mirrors, and
     corporate CAs.


